      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T16:29:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My preference would be to initialize it here for two reasons:\n\n1. The reader can convince themselves that this is safe by looking at only at this particular function. As it stands, they have to look up the definition of `kvm_iommu_map_pages` which is in a different file. Also, if someone were to edit `kvm_iommu_map_pages`, they might not realize that the caller relies on this initialization.\n\n2. Initializing `mapped` here would align with `__iommu_map` in `drivers/iommu/iommu.c` which initializes `mapped`, because the callee doesn\u0027t necessarily write to it in error conditions.",
      "parentUuid": "b640ba16_9484ea10",
      "revId": "980023c79df574d1407b670329297029e840013f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
